.TH sort 1 (date) "GNU coreutils (unreleased)"
.SH NAME
sort \- sort lines of text files
.SH SYNOPSIS
.SY sort
.RI [ OPTION \~.\|.\|.\&]
.RI [ FILE \~.\|.\|.\&]
.YS
.SY sort
.RI [ OPTION \~.\|.\|.\&]
.BI \-\-files0\-from= F
.YS
.SH DESCRIPTION
.\" Add any additional description here
.PP
Write sorted concatenation of all FILE(s) to standard output.
.PP
With no FILE, or when FILE is \-, read standard input.
.PP
Mandatory arguments to long options are mandatory for short options too.
Ordering options:
.TP
.UR https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#sort\-b
\fB\-b, \-\-ignore\-leading\-blanks\fP
.UE
ignore leading blanks when finding sort keys in each line
.TP
.UR https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#sort\-d
\fB\-d, \-\-dictionary\-order\fP
.UE
consider only blanks and alphanumeric characters
.TP
.UR https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#sort\-f
\fB\-f, \-\-ignore\-case\fP
.UE
fold lower case to upper case characters
.TP
.UR https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#sort\-g
\fB\-g, \-\-general\-numeric\-sort\fP
.UE
compare according to general numerical value
.TP
.UR https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#sort\-i
\fB\-i, \-\-ignore\-nonprinting\fP
.UE
consider only printable characters
.TP
.UR https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#sort\-M
\fB\-M, \-\-month\-sort\fP
.UE
compare (unknown) < 'JAN' < ... < 'DEC'
.TP
.UR https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#sort\-h
\fB\-h, \-\-human\-numeric\-sort\fP
.UE
compare human readable numbers (e.g., 2K 1G)
.TP
.UR https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#sort\-n
\fB\-n, \-\-numeric\-sort\fP
.UE
compare according to string numerical value;
see full documentation for supported strings
.TP
.UR https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#sort\-R
\fB\-R, \-\-random\-sort\fP
.UE
shuffle, but group identical keys.  See also \fBshuf\fP(1)
.TP
.UR https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#sort\-\-random\-source
\fB\-\-random\-source=FILE\fP
.UE
get random bytes from FILE
.TP
.UR https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#sort\-r
\fB\-r, \-\-reverse\fP
.UE
reverse the result of comparisons
.TP
.UR https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#sort\-\-sort
\fB\-\-sort=WORD\fP
.UE
sort according to WORD:
general\-numeric \fB\-g\fR, human\-numeric \fB\-h\fR, month \fB\-M\fR,
numeric \fB\-n\fR, random \fB\-R\fR, version \fB\-V\fR
.TP
.UR https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#sort\-V
\fB\-V, \-\-version\-sort\fP
.UE
natural sort of (version) numbers within text
.PP
Other options:
.TP
.UR https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#sort\-\-batch\-size
\fB\-\-batch\-size=NMERGE\fP
.UE
merge at most NMERGE inputs at once; for more use temp files
.TP
.UR https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#sort\-c
\fB\-c, \-\-check, \-\-check=\,diagnose\-first\fP
.UE
check for sorted input; do not sort
.TP
.UR https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#sort\-C
\fB\-C, \-\-check=\,quiet\/, \-\-check=\,silent\fP
.UE
like \fB\-c\fR, but do not report first bad line
.TP
.UR https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#sort\-\-compress\-program
\fB\-\-compress\-program=PROG\fP
.UE
compress temporaries with PROG; decompress them with PROG \fB\-d\fR
.TP
.UR https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#sort\-\-debug
\fB\-\-debug\fP
.UE
annotate the part of the line used to sort,
and warn about questionable usage to standard error
.TP
.UR https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#sort\-\-files0\-from
\fB\-\-files0\-from=F\fP
.UE
read input from the files specified by NUL\-terminated names in file F;
If F is \-, read names from standard input
.TP
.UR https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#sort\-k
\fB\-k, \-\-key=\,KEYDEF\fP
.UE
sort via a key; KEYDEF gives location and type
.TP
.UR https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#sort\-m
\fB\-m, \-\-merge\fP
.UE
merge already sorted files; do not sort
.TP
.UR https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#sort\-o
\fB\-o, \-\-output=\,FILE\fP
.UE
write result to FILE instead of standard output
.TP
.UR https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#sort\-s
\fB\-s, \-\-stable\fP
.UE
stabilize sort by disabling last\-resort comparison
.TP
.UR https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#sort\-S
\fB\-S, \-\-buffer\-size=\,SIZE\fP
.UE
use SIZE for main memory buffer
.TP
.UR https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#sort\-t
\fB\-t, \-\-field\-separator=\,SEP\fP
.UE
use SEP instead of non\-blank to blank transition
.TP
.UR https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#sort\-T
\fB\-T, \-\-temporary\-directory=\,DIR\fP
.UE
use DIR for temporaries, not $TMPDIR or \fI\,/tmp\/\fP;
multiple options specify multiple directories
.TP
.UR https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#sort\-\-parallel
\fB\-\-parallel=N\fP
.UE
change the number of sorts run concurrently to N
.TP
.UR https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#sort\-u
\fB\-u, \-\-unique\fP
.UE
output only the first of lines with equal keys;
with \fB\-c\fR, check for strict ordering
.TP
.UR https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#sort\-z
\fB\-z, \-\-zero\-terminated\fP
.UE
line delimiter is NUL, not newline
.TP
.UR https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/sort#sort\-\-help
\fB\-\-help\fP
.UE
display this help and exit
.TP
.UR https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/sort#sort\-\-version
\fB\-\-version\fP
.UE
output version information and exit
.PP
KEYDEF is F[.C][OPTS][,F[.C][OPTS]] for start and stop position, where F is a
field number and C a character position in the field; both are origin 1, and
the stop position defaults to the line's end.  If neither \fB\-t\fR nor \fB\-b\fR is in
effect, characters in a field are counted from the beginning of the preceding
whitespace.  OPTS is one or more single\-letter ordering options [bdfgiMhnRrV],
which override global ordering options for that key.  If no key is given, use
the entire line as the key.  Use \fB\-\-debug\fR to diagnose incorrect key usage.
.PP
SIZE may be followed by the following multiplicative suffixes:
% 1% of memory, b 1, K 1024 (default), and so on for M, G, T, P, E, Z, Y, R, Q.
.PP
*** WARNING ***
The locale specified by the environment affects sort order.
Set LC_ALL=C to get the traditional sort order that uses
native byte values.
